Rule 1 (tensor shapes should be the same)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)
>>
Rule 3 (tensor dimensions should be valid for tensordot)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : int} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ v_3 ∧ ndim(v_2) ≥ v_3 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, v_3 - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)
>>
Rule 6 (tensor dimensions should match for tensordot)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : list(int)} |= v_3.len = 2 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)
>>
Rule 7 (tensor dimensions should be valid for tensordot)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tuple(int)} |= v_3.len = 2 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)
